## Status

**Every source file in this repository is this project's own code.**

Measured, not asserted. `tools/accept_rewrite.py` strips comments and normalises
whitespace from each file, then compares it against its upstream baseline; the count that
still matches is the number of files carrying upstream code. For this repository that
count is **0 of 75**.

The same run regenerates all 27 differential fixtures from the live TypeScript and diffs
them against frozen golden copies — 27 of 27 byte-identical. That pairing is the point:
the code changed, and its observable behaviour did not.

## What the project is

**Bannerlord-Blore** (MCP name `blore`) — a Bannerlord MCP server exposing `ba_*` tools
for mod development: XML / decompiled-source / README indexing with SQLite + FTS5, entity
lookups with localization resolution, mod-source C# indexing, cross-session project
memory, path-sandboxed file access, workspace scaffolding, Harmony/XSLT patch generators,
and a doctor/verify toolchain.

